r we wrote and have determined it must be happening somewhere in gRPC. I've included a simple script to reproduce the problem quite quickly in python. Note sure how to track down the leak or if it's on the python side or in the C core. We have tried replacing the worker queue with a different one (not concurrent.futures thread pool) and that didn't help. We also switched to a different simple python RPC  service ([speedy](https://github.com/rjpower/speedy)) and that completely fixes the problem. \n\nI've attached a zip of requirements.txt (just futures, grpc and proto), compiled proto and client / server setup. The server can run with a simple client sending requests in a loop and the server will leak. The bigger the request size the faster it leaks. The server will print out the memory for you (or you can watch it increase in top). Here is how you run the server: \n\n```\npython leaky/server.py --port 3000 --pool_size 100 --run_client_here 1\n```\n\nYou can also run the client and server separately: \n\n```\npython leaky/server.py --port 3000 --pool_size 100 \n```\n\n```\npython leaky/client.py\n```\n\n[leaky.zip](https://github.com/grpc/grpc/files/184639/leaky.zip)\n","closed_by":{"login":"jtattermusch","id":9939684,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5Mzk2ODQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9939684?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jtattermusch","html_url":"https://github.com/jtattermusch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jtattermusch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jtattermusch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jtattermusch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jtattermusch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jtattermusch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jtattermusch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jtattermusch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.co